WEBVTT

00:02.509 --> 00:03.760
KATARA: Water...

00:04.886 --> 00:06.137
Earth...

00:06.846 --> 00:08.139
Fire...

00:08.848 --> 00:10.183
Air.

00:11.017 --> 00:14.229
Long ago, the four nations
lived together in harmony.

00:15.146 --> 00:19.067
Then everything changed
when the fire nation attacked.

00:19.400 --> 00:23.613
Only the Avatar, master of
all four elements, could stop them.

00:23.696 --> 00:25.448
But when the world
needed him most

00:25.532 --> 00:27.408
he vanished.

00:27.492 --> 00:31.079
100 years passed and my brother
and I discovered the new Avatar

00:31.162 --> 00:32.789
an Airbender named Aang.

00:32.872 --> 00:35.208
And although his airbending
skills are great

00:35.291 --> 00:37.669
he has a lot to learn before
he's ready to save anyone.

00:37.752 --> 00:38.753
AANG: Oof.

00:38.878 --> 00:42.882
But I believe Aang
can save the world.

00:42.966 --> 00:46.469
[ ♪... ]

00:48.054 --> 00:50.515
( MAN READING )

00:50.598 --> 00:54.435
You're looking at the only Waterbender
in the whole south pole.

00:55.228 --> 00:58.523
This ship has haunted my tribe
since gran-gran was a little girl.

00:58.606 --> 01:01.985
It was part of
the Fire Nation's first attack.

01:02.068 --> 01:05.280
WOMAN: The legends say the moon
was the first Waterbender.

01:05.530 --> 01:07.615
Our ancestors saw how it
pushed and pulled the tides

01:07.699 --> 01:09.867
and learned how to
do it themselves.

01:09.951 --> 01:13.037
KATARA: I've always noticed
my waterbending is stronger at night.

01:15.790 --> 01:17.041
TOPH: What are you doing?

01:17.125 --> 01:19.252
KATARA: I'm making my own water.

01:22.005 --> 01:24.424
[ ♪... ]

01:27.302 --> 01:29.220
[ Crickets Chirping... ]

01:38.771 --> 01:41.608
Suddenly, they heard something
down the hall, in the dark.

01:42.400 --> 01:45.570
♪Ooh... ♪

01:46.154 --> 01:48.698
It came into the torchlight.

01:49.365 --> 01:53.119
And they knew the blade
of Wing-fun was haunted!

01:53.870 --> 01:57.957
♪Ah-ah... ♪

01:59.083 --> 02:02.462
I think I liked "The Man
With a Sword for a Hand" better.

02:02.545 --> 02:05.298
Water tribe slumber parties
must stink.

02:05.840 --> 02:07.383
No, wait, I've got one.

02:07.467 --> 02:09.844
And this is a true southern
Water tribe story.

02:10.136 --> 02:11.888
Is this one of those
"a friend of my cousin

02:11.971 --> 02:14.557
knew some guy that
this happened to" story?

02:14.849 --> 02:17.268
No, it happened to Mom.

02:20.146 --> 02:22.315
One winter, when Mom was a girl

02:22.398 --> 02:25.234
a snowstorm buried
the whole village for weeks.

02:25.318 --> 02:29.572
A month later, mom realized she hadn't
seen her friend Nini since the storm.

02:29.656 --> 02:32.784
So Mom and some others
went to check on Nini's family.

02:32.867 --> 02:34.911
When they got there,
no one was home.

02:34.994 --> 02:37.580
Just a fire
flickering in the fireplace.

02:37.664 --> 02:39.624
While the men
went out to search

02:39.707 --> 02:41.167
Mom stayed in the house.

02:41.250 --> 02:44.253
When she was alone,
she heard a voice.

02:44.337 --> 02:48.925
"It's so cold,
and I can't get warm."

02:49.008 --> 02:52.178
Mom turned and saw
Nini standing by the fire.

02:52.261 --> 02:54.681
She was blue,
like she was frozen.

02:54.764 --> 02:58.643
Mom ran outside for help,
but when every one came back

02:58.726 --> 03:00.561
Nini was gone.

03:00.853 --> 03:02.355
SOKKA: Where'd she go?

03:02.772 --> 03:04.148
No one knows.

03:04.232 --> 03:06.901
Nini's house stands empty
to this day.

03:06.984 --> 03:09.904
But sometimes, people see smoke
coming up from the chimney

03:09.987 --> 03:13.491
like little Nini is still
trying to get warm.

03:16.911 --> 03:18.538
[ Gasps ]
Wait.

03:18.621 --> 03:20.707
Guys, did you hear that?

03:20.998 --> 03:24.377
I hear people under the mountain,
and they're screaming.

03:25.670 --> 03:27.463
Pft, nice try.

03:27.839 --> 03:30.675
TOPH: No, I'm serious,
I hear something.

03:30.758 --> 03:33.886
KATARA: You're probably just
jumpy from the ghost stories.

03:34.554 --> 03:36.305
TOPH: It just stopped.

03:36.389 --> 03:38.516
All right, now
I'm getting scared.

03:38.933 --> 03:40.351
WOMAN: Hello, children.

03:40.435 --> 03:42.145
[ Screaming ]

03:44.939 --> 03:48.151
Sorry to frighten you,
my name is Hama.

03:48.234 --> 03:52.238
You children shouldn't be out in
the forest by yourselves at night.

03:52.530 --> 03:56.117
I have an inn nearby,
why don't you come back there

03:56.200 --> 03:58.327
for some spiced tea and warm beds?

03:59.162 --> 04:00.997
Yes, please.

04:08.296 --> 04:11.215
Thanks for letting us stay here tonight,
you have a lovely inn.

04:11.299 --> 04:13.176
Aren't you sweet?

04:13.259 --> 04:14.886
You know, you should be careful.

04:14.969 --> 04:18.473
People have been disappearing in
those woods you were camping in.

04:18.806 --> 04:20.475
What do you mean, disappearing?

04:20.850 --> 04:25.146
When the moon turns full,
people walk in

04:25.229 --> 04:28.399
and they don't come out.

04:28.483 --> 04:30.860
Who wants more tea?

04:34.822 --> 04:38.201
Don't worry, you'll all be
completely safe here.

04:38.284 --> 04:43.039
Why don't I show you to your rooms,
and you can get a good night's rest?

04:45.291 --> 04:47.084
[ Wood Creaks ]

04:47.168 --> 04:48.669
[ Grunts ]

04:48.878 --> 04:50.546
[ Wood Creaks ]

04:51.172 --> 04:52.673
[ Gasps ]

04:53.591 --> 04:55.927
I know, Momo,
this place is creepy.

04:56.135 --> 04:58.471
I don't know if I'm
gonna be able to fall asleep.

04:59.055 --> 05:02.058
[ Snoring... ]

05:04.852 --> 05:07.063
[ Birds Chirping ]

05:08.564 --> 05:10.566
HAMA: Wakey-wakey.

05:11.108 --> 05:13.402
Time to go shopping.

05:23.663 --> 05:25.957
That Mr. Yao seems to
have a thing for you.

05:26.040 --> 05:29.293
Maybe we should go back and see if he'll
give us some free komodo sausages.

05:29.877 --> 05:33.256
You would have me use
my feminine charms

05:33.339 --> 05:35.591
to take advantage
of that poor man?

05:35.675 --> 05:39.428
I think you and I are
going to get along swimmingly.

05:39.512 --> 05:42.557
You won't have any
ash bananas till next week?

05:43.349 --> 05:46.561
Well, I have to send the boy
to Hing-wa Island to get them,

05:46.644 --> 05:47.687
and it's a two-day trip.

05:47.770 --> 05:51.148
Oh, right, tomorrow's
the full moon.

05:51.232 --> 05:54.485
Exactly, I can't lose another
delivery boy in the woods.

05:55.236 --> 05:57.154
People disappearing
in the woods,

05:57.238 --> 05:59.031
weird stuff during full moons,

05:59.115 --> 06:01.826
this just reeks of
spirit world shenanigans.

06:01.909 --> 06:04.245
I bet if we take
a little walk around town

06:04.328 --> 06:07.498
we'll find out what these people did to
the environment to make the spirits mad.

06:07.582 --> 06:11.669
And then you can sew up this little
mystery, lickety-split, Avatar-style.

06:11.752 --> 06:14.213
Helping people,
that's what I do.

06:15.089 --> 06:18.384
HAMA: Why don't you all take
those things back to the inn?

06:18.551 --> 06:20.761
I just have to run
a couple more errands.

06:20.845 --> 06:22.930
I'll be back in a little while.

06:23.389 --> 06:25.391
This is a mysterious,
little town you have here.

06:26.517 --> 06:29.770
Mysterious town
for mysterious children.

06:36.986 --> 06:38.946
That Hama seems a little strange.

06:39.030 --> 06:41.574
Like she knows something,
or she's hiding something.

06:41.657 --> 06:43.284
That's ridiculous.

06:43.367 --> 06:46.412
She's a nice woman who took us
in and gave us a place to stay.

06:46.495 --> 06:48.122
She kind of reminds me
of gran-gran.

06:48.497 --> 06:51.584
But what did she mean by that comment
"mysterious children"?

06:51.876 --> 06:53.294
Gee, I don't know.

06:53.377 --> 06:57.340
Maybe because she found four strange kids
camping in the woods at night?

06:57.673 --> 07:00.217
Isn't that a little mysterious?

07:00.551 --> 07:02.887
I'm gonna take a look around.

07:05.556 --> 07:07.850
Sokka, Sokka,
what are you doing?

07:07.934 --> 07:10.311
You can't just snoop around
someone's house.

07:10.394 --> 07:11.395
SOKKA: It'll be fine.

07:11.479 --> 07:14.023
AANG: She could be home
any minute.

07:14.982 --> 07:17.526
Sokka, you're gonna get us
all in trouble.

07:17.610 --> 07:19.320
And this is just plain rude.

07:19.403 --> 07:20.863
I'm not finished yet.

07:20.988 --> 07:23.491
[ Grunts ]
Come on...

07:24.867 --> 07:27.036
[ Screams ]

07:27.119 --> 07:29.288
AANG: Ok, that's pretty creepy.

07:29.538 --> 07:31.374
So she's got a hobby.

07:31.457 --> 07:32.917
There's nothing
weird about that.

07:33.000 --> 07:34.794
Sokka, you've looked enough.

07:34.877 --> 07:36.587
Hama will be back soon.

07:36.671 --> 07:38.089
[ Sokka Grunts ]

07:38.172 --> 07:40.257
Just an ordinary, puppet-loving
innkeeper, huh?

07:40.341 --> 07:42.218
Then why does she have
a locked door up here?

07:42.301 --> 07:45.763
Probably to keep people like you
from snooping through her stuff.

07:45.846 --> 07:47.974
SOKKA: We'll see.

07:48.057 --> 07:49.809
It's empty except for
a little chest.

07:49.892 --> 07:53.396
[ Gasps ]
Maybe it's treasure.

07:53.479 --> 07:55.439
Sokka, what are you doing?

07:55.523 --> 07:57.400
You're breaking into
a private room.

07:57.483 --> 07:59.735
I have to see what's in there.

08:02.905 --> 08:05.408
We shouldn't be doing this.

08:05.908 --> 08:08.160
Maybe there's a key
here somewhere.

08:08.244 --> 08:09.996
Oh, hand it over.

08:14.709 --> 08:16.335
Come on, come on.

08:16.419 --> 08:18.546
This isn't as easy it looks.

08:18.879 --> 08:20.631
AANG: Guys, I don't know
about this.

08:20.715 --> 08:22.800
This is crazy, I'm leaving.

08:22.883 --> 08:24.677
Suit yourself, do it, Toph.

08:28.305 --> 08:30.599
HAMA: I'll tell you
what's in the box.

08:45.781 --> 08:47.450
An old comb?

08:47.533 --> 08:50.453
It's my greatest treasure.

08:50.536 --> 08:55.041
It's the last thing I owned from
growing up in the southern Water tribe.

08:59.712 --> 09:01.714
You're from the southern
Water tribe?

09:02.548 --> 09:03.883
Just like you.

09:03.966 --> 09:05.301
How did you know?

09:05.384 --> 09:07.678
I heard you talking
around your campfire.

09:07.762 --> 09:09.597
But why didn't you tell us?

09:09.680 --> 09:11.766
I wanted to surprise you.

09:11.849 --> 09:16.479
I bought all this food today so I could
fix you a big, Water Tribe dinner.

09:16.729 --> 09:19.899
Of course, I can't get all
the ingredients I need here, but

09:20.066 --> 09:24.195
ocean kumquats are a lot like sea prunes,
if you stew them long enough.

09:24.278 --> 09:25.404
[ Gags ]

09:25.488 --> 09:26.530
Great.

09:26.655 --> 09:28.824
I knew I felt a bond
with you right away.

09:29.241 --> 09:30.910
And I knew you were
keeping a secret

09:30.993 --> 09:32.828
so I guess we're both right.

09:32.912 --> 09:35.748
[ Grunts ] But I'm sorry we were
sneaking around.

09:35.915 --> 09:37.625
Apology accepted.

09:38.501 --> 09:40.127
Now let's get cooking.

09:49.970 --> 09:52.556
[ Momo Chirps ]

09:59.563 --> 10:01.941
I'd steer clear
of the sea prunes.

10:02.066 --> 10:04.360
I thought they were
ocean kumquats.

10:04.443 --> 10:05.528
Close enough.

10:05.653 --> 10:08.447
Who wants five-flavor soup?

10:13.452 --> 10:14.578
You're a Waterbender.

10:14.662 --> 10:17.373
I've never met another
Waterbender from our tribe.

10:17.456 --> 10:21.043
That's because the Fire Nation
wiped them all out.

10:21.502 --> 10:23.087
I was the last one.

10:23.337 --> 10:25.089
So how did you end up out here?

10:26.090 --> 10:28.592
I was stolen from my home.

10:30.052 --> 10:33.639
It was over 60 years ago
when the raids started.

10:34.473 --> 10:36.058
[ Laughing ]

10:56.203 --> 10:57.621
[ Man Screams ]

11:00.666 --> 11:02.418
HAMA: They came again and again.

11:02.793 --> 11:07.381
Each time, rounding up more of our
Waterbenders and taking them captive.

11:07.882 --> 11:10.134
[ Breathing Heavily ]

11:11.677 --> 11:13.470
We did our best to hold them off

11:13.554 --> 11:17.558
but our numbers dwindled
as the raids continued.

11:25.649 --> 11:29.236
Finally, I, too, was captured.

11:30.821 --> 11:33.032
I was led away in chains.

11:34.450 --> 11:38.454
The last Waterbender of
the southern Water Tribe.

11:45.461 --> 11:49.256
They put us in terrible prisons
here in the Fire Nation.

11:49.590 --> 11:52.968
I was the only one
who managed to escape.

11:53.052 --> 11:54.595
How did you get away?

11:54.678 --> 11:56.472
And why did you stay
in the Fire Nation?

11:57.097 --> 11:58.557
I'm sorry.

11:58.641 --> 12:01.727
It's too painful to
talk about anymore.

12:01.810 --> 12:03.687
We completely understand.

12:03.771 --> 12:05.898
We lost our mother in a raid.

12:06.232 --> 12:08.525
Oh, you poor things.

12:10.945 --> 12:13.447
I can't tell you
what it means to meet you.

12:13.530 --> 12:15.950
It's an honor, you're a hero.

12:16.325 --> 12:19.536
I never thought I'd meet
another southern Waterbender.

12:19.787 --> 12:21.830
I'd like to teach you
what I know

12:21.914 --> 12:25.167
so you can carry on the southern tradition
when I'm gone.

12:25.584 --> 12:28.379
Yes, yes, of course.

12:28.837 --> 12:32.258
To learn about my heritage,
it would mean everything to me.

12:36.845 --> 12:38.889
HAMA: Growing up
at the south pole

12:38.973 --> 12:43.852
Waterbenders are totally at home
surrounded by snow and ice and seas.

12:44.395 --> 12:46.897
But as you probably
noticed on your travels,

12:46.981 --> 12:49.233
that isn't the case
wherever you go.

12:49.483 --> 12:51.819
I know, when we were
stranded in the desert

12:51.902 --> 12:54.571
I felt like there was
almost nothing I could do.

12:54.655 --> 12:58.659
That's why you have to learn to
control water wherever it exists.

12:58.951 --> 13:01.537
I've even used my own
sweat for waterbending.

13:01.704 --> 13:04.081
That's very resourceful, Katara.

13:04.206 --> 13:06.583
You're thinking like
a true master.

13:06.667 --> 13:10.045
But did you know you can even
pull water out of thin air?

13:14.258 --> 13:17.303
You've got to
keep an open mind, Katara.

13:18.220 --> 13:21.056
There's water in places
you never think about.

13:25.644 --> 13:28.689
AANG: This has gotta be the nicest,
natural setting in the Fire Nation.

13:29.023 --> 13:31.483
I don't see anything that would
make a spirit mad around here.

13:31.775 --> 13:34.737
Maybe the moon spirit
just turned mean.

13:35.112 --> 13:38.073
The moon spirit is
a gentle, loving lady.

13:38.157 --> 13:40.326
She rules the sky
with compassion.

13:40.409 --> 13:42.578
And... Lunar goodness.

13:44.330 --> 13:46.123
AANG: Excuse me, sir.

13:46.248 --> 13:49.293
Can you tell us anything about
the spirit that's been stealing people?

13:49.585 --> 13:53.756
Only one man ever saw it and
lived, and that's old man Ding.

13:53.839 --> 13:56.300
Where does old man Ding live?

13:56.383 --> 13:59.636
KATARA: Wow, these flowers
are beautiful.

13:59.762 --> 14:01.680
HAMA: They're called fire lilies.

14:01.764 --> 14:04.725
They only bloom
a few weeks a year

14:04.808 --> 14:08.228
but they're one of my favorite
things about living here.

14:08.312 --> 14:12.149
And like all plants, and all
living things, they're filled with water.

14:12.816 --> 14:14.985
I met a waterbender
who lived in a swamp

14:15.110 --> 14:17.613
and could control the vines
by bending the water inside.

14:18.322 --> 14:20.741
You can take it even further.

14:27.664 --> 14:29.666
That was incredible.

14:31.001 --> 14:33.087
It's a shame about
the lilies, though.

14:33.212 --> 14:34.713
They're just flowers.

14:35.214 --> 14:37.466
When you're a waterbender
in a strange land

14:37.549 --> 14:40.010
you do what you must to survive.

14:40.219 --> 14:43.680
Tonight, I'll teach you the ultimate
technique of waterbending.

14:43.847 --> 14:46.975
It can only be done
during the full moon

14:47.059 --> 14:49.186
when your bending
is at its peak.

14:49.353 --> 14:51.355
But isn't that dangerous?

14:51.480 --> 14:54.608
I thought people have been disappearing
around here during the full moon.

14:54.942 --> 14:56.402
Oh, Katara.

14:56.610 --> 15:00.114
Two master Waterbenders
beneath a full moon?

15:00.197 --> 15:03.033
I don't think we have
anything to worry about.

15:13.293 --> 15:14.294
AANG: Old man Ding?

15:14.378 --> 15:16.296
Eh, ow...

15:16.380 --> 15:17.673
Aw, dad blame it.

15:17.756 --> 15:18.924
What?

15:19.007 --> 15:20.634
Can't you see I'm busy?

15:20.717 --> 15:22.803
Got a full moon rising.

15:22.886 --> 15:26.765
And why does everyone
call me that, I'm not that old.

15:26.849 --> 15:28.809
[ Grunts ]

15:29.017 --> 15:30.436
Aww...

15:30.519 --> 15:32.479
Well, I'm young at heart.

15:35.899 --> 15:40.988
Not ready to get snapped up
by some moon monster, yet, at least.

15:41.071 --> 15:43.323
SOKKA: We wanted to
ask you about that.

15:43.407 --> 15:45.284
Did you get a good look
at the spirit that took you?

15:45.367 --> 15:47.161
Didn't see no spirit.

15:47.244 --> 15:49.413
Just felt something
come over me.

15:49.496 --> 15:51.331
Like I was possessed.

15:51.415 --> 15:55.419
Forced me to start
walking toward the mountain.

15:55.752 --> 15:59.298
I tried to fight it, but
I couldn't control my own limbs.

16:00.132 --> 16:03.010
It just about had me
into a cave up there.

16:03.093 --> 16:08.807
And I looked up at the moon for what I
thought would be my last glimpse of light.

16:09.975 --> 16:13.270
But then the sun
started to rise.

16:13.353 --> 16:15.647
And I got control of
myself again.

16:15.731 --> 16:19.151
I just high-tailed it away from
that mountain as quick as I could.

16:19.234 --> 16:21.820
Why would a spirit want to
take people to a mountain?

16:21.904 --> 16:23.030
Oh, no!

16:23.113 --> 16:25.532
I did hear people screaming
under the mountain.

16:25.616 --> 16:28.327
The missing villagers
must still be there.

16:40.255 --> 16:42.466
I can hear them,
they're this way.

16:46.845 --> 16:50.098
HAMA: Can you feel the power
the full moon brings?

16:50.182 --> 16:52.559
[ Breathes Deeply ]

16:52.643 --> 16:56.855
For generations, it has blessed
Waterbenders with its glow.

16:56.939 --> 17:00.359
Allowing us to do
incredible things.

17:02.528 --> 17:05.489
I've never felt more alive.

17:10.160 --> 17:11.495
This is the place.

17:11.578 --> 17:13.539
SOKKA: I can't see
anything down there.

17:13.622 --> 17:15.624
TOPH: That's why you have me,
let's go.

17:29.221 --> 17:31.098
We're saved.

17:31.181 --> 17:35.686
I didn't know that spirits made prisons
like this, who brought you here?

17:35.769 --> 17:37.229
It was no spirit.

17:37.312 --> 17:38.939
It was a witch.

17:39.022 --> 17:41.024
A witch, what do you mean?

17:41.108 --> 17:44.027
She seems like
a normal old woman.

17:44.111 --> 17:47.739
But she controls people
like some dark puppetmaster.

17:47.823 --> 17:49.241
Hama.

17:49.324 --> 17:51.368
Yes, the innkeeper.

17:51.451 --> 17:54.162
I knew there was something
creepy about her.

17:54.329 --> 17:55.789
We have to stop Hama.

17:55.872 --> 17:59.209
I'll get these people
out of here, you go.

17:59.293 --> 18:01.920
[ Owl Hoots ]

18:04.339 --> 18:06.133
HAMA: What I'm about to show you

18:06.216 --> 18:09.553
I discovered in that
wretched, Fire Nation prison.

18:10.679 --> 18:14.391
The guards were always careful
to keep any water away from us.

18:14.641 --> 18:18.770
They piped in dry air, and had us
suspended away from the ground.

18:19.354 --> 18:21.064
Before giving us any water,

18:21.148 --> 18:24.526
they would bind our hands and feet
so we couldn't bend.

18:24.610 --> 18:28.488
Any sign of trouble
was met with cruel retribution.

18:29.364 --> 18:33.785
And yet, each month, I felt the full moon
enriching me with its energy.

18:34.244 --> 18:37.623
There had to be something
I could do to escape.

18:37.789 --> 18:42.461
Then I realized that where
there is life, there is water.

18:42.753 --> 18:46.089
The rats that scurried across
the floor of my cage

18:46.173 --> 18:49.509
were nothing more than
skins filled with liquid.

18:49.593 --> 18:54.473
And I passed years developing the skills
that would lead to my escape.

18:55.515 --> 18:57.517
Bloodbending.

18:57.976 --> 19:00.771
Controlling the water
in another body.

19:00.854 --> 19:03.815
Enforcing your own will
over theirs.

19:04.399 --> 19:09.529
Once I had mastered the rats,
I was ready for the men.

19:09.613 --> 19:13.116
[ Grunts ]

19:16.119 --> 19:18.372
HAMA: And during the next
full moon,

19:18.455 --> 19:21.249
I walked free for
the first time in decades.

19:21.333 --> 19:22.501
[ Man Grunts ]

19:22.584 --> 19:26.838
My cell unlocked by the very
guards assigned to keep me in.

19:27.839 --> 19:32.260
Once you perfect this technique,
you can control anything.

19:32.344 --> 19:34.763
Or anyone.

19:34.846 --> 19:38.642
But to reach inside someone
and control them?

19:38.975 --> 19:41.645
I don't know if I want
that kind of power.

19:41.728 --> 19:44.272
The choice is not yours.

19:44.356 --> 19:46.191
The power exists.

19:46.566 --> 19:50.779
And it's your duty to use the gifts
you've been given to win this war.

19:50.862 --> 19:56.243
Katara, they tried to wipe us out,
our entire culture, your mother.

19:56.326 --> 19:57.661
I know.

19:57.828 --> 20:01.289
Then you should understand
what I'm talking about.

20:01.373 --> 20:04.501
We're the last Waterbenders
of the southern tribe.

20:04.584 --> 20:07.713
We have to fight these people
whenever we can.

20:07.796 --> 20:11.133
Wherever they are,
with any means necessary.

20:12.134 --> 20:13.510
It's you.

20:13.593 --> 20:16.930
You're the one who's making people
disappear during the full moons.

20:17.347 --> 20:20.267
They threw me in prison to rot

20:20.350 --> 20:22.686
along with
my brothers and sisters.

20:22.769 --> 20:24.354
They deserve the same.

20:24.730 --> 20:26.732
You must carry on my work.

20:26.815 --> 20:29.234
I won't, I won't
use bloodbending

20:29.317 --> 20:32.028
and I won't allow you
to keep terrorizing this town.

20:32.112 --> 20:33.613
[ Screams ]

20:33.697 --> 20:36.199
[ Grunts... ]

20:36.283 --> 20:40.203
You should have learned the technique
before you turned against me.

20:40.287 --> 20:43.582
It's impossible to fight
your way out of my grip.

20:43.707 --> 20:48.253
I control every muscle,
every vein in your body.

20:48.336 --> 20:53.008
[ Katara Gasps and grunts... ]

21:01.266 --> 21:03.018
Stop, please.

21:03.101 --> 21:08.148
[ Laughs... ]

21:21.244 --> 21:24.331
KATARA: You're not the only one
who draws power from the moon.

21:24.456 --> 21:27.250
My bending is more powerful
than yours, Hama.

21:27.334 --> 21:30.545
Your technique is useless on me.

21:49.356 --> 21:51.441
[ Hama Screams ]

21:54.986 --> 21:56.655
We know what you've
been doing, Hama.

21:56.988 --> 21:58.782
Give up, you're outnumbered.

21:59.366 --> 22:00.909
No.

22:01.701 --> 22:04.496
You've outnumbered yourselves.

22:04.663 --> 22:08.124
[ Aang And Sokka scream ]

22:13.755 --> 22:15.257
SOKKA: Katara, look out!

22:15.465 --> 22:17.342
[ Grunts ]

22:17.509 --> 22:20.136
It's like my brain
has a mind of its own.

22:20.303 --> 22:22.347
Stop it, arm, stop it!

22:25.350 --> 22:27.102
AANG: This feels weird.

22:27.185 --> 22:29.980
[ Aang Grunts ]

22:30.063 --> 22:31.898
I'm sorry, Aang.

22:31.982 --> 22:33.567
AANG: It's ok.

22:36.152 --> 22:39.281
[ Sokka Grunts ]

22:39.364 --> 22:40.949
[ Sokka Screams ]

22:41.032 --> 22:43.535
Don't hurt your friends, Katara.

22:43.618 --> 22:46.162
And don't let them
hurt each other.

22:46.246 --> 22:48.498
[ Aang And Sokka scream ]

22:48.582 --> 22:49.875
No!

22:54.254 --> 22:58.174
[ Grunts And gasps... ]

23:11.771 --> 23:14.566
You're going to be
locked away forever.

23:14.649 --> 23:16.943
HAMA: My work is done.

23:17.777 --> 23:20.155
Congratulations, Katara.

23:20.780 --> 23:22.991
You're a bloodbender.

23:24.784 --> 23:28.538
[ Laughs... ]

23:32.208 --> 23:36.212
[ Katara Cries... ]

23:44.763 --> 23:49.309
[ ♪... ]
